{"name":"Restoration","hex":"#939581","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Restoration","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The events of 1660 when English, Scottish and Irish monarchies were restored under Charles II.","The era of Restoration (1660 to 1685) under Charles II, or to 1688 when James II was king."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Restoration"}],"entries":[{"title":"Conservation and restoration of cultural property","blocks":[{"text":"The conservation and restoration of cultural property focuses on protection and care of cultural property, including artworks, architecture, archaeology, and museum collections. Conservation activities include preventive conservation, examination, documentation, research, treatment, and education. This field is closely allied with conservation science, curators and registrars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/97/Conservation_at_the_Church_of_Sucevi%C5%A3a.jpg/330px-Conservation_at_the_Church_of_Sucevi%C5%A3a.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conservation_and_restoration_of_cultural_property","wikidata":"Q46993143"},{"title":"Audio restoration","blocks":[{"text":"Audio restoration is the process of removing imperfections from sound recordings. Audio restoration can be performed directly on the recording medium or on a digital representation of the recording using a computer. Record restoration\nis a particular form of audio restoration that seeks to repair the sound of damaged gramophone records."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/DC8Screen.jpg/330px-DC8Screen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Audio_restoration","wikidata":"Q4819882"},{"title":"Restoration (Scotland)","blocks":[{"text":"The Restoration was the return of the monarchy to Scotland in 1660 after the period of the Commonwealth, and the subsequent three decades of Scottish history until the Revolution and Convention of Estates of 1689. It was part of a wider Restoration in the British Isles that included the return of the Stuart dynasty to the thrones of England and Ireland in the person of Charles II."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Charles_II_of_England.jpeg/330px-Charles_II_of_England.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Restoration_(Scotland)","wikidata":"Q7316198"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/HorsesSaintMark1.jpg/500px-HorsesSaintMark1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/HorsesSaintMark1.jpg/1280px-HorsesSaintMark1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/HorsesSaintMark1.jpg/500px-HorsesSaintMark1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Conservation of the Horses of Saint Mark (Venice)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHorsesSaintMark1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Holy_Trinity_Column_2006_conservation_3.jpg/500px-Holy_Trinity_Column_2006_conservation_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Holy_Trinity_Column_2006_conservation_3.jpg/1280px-Holy_Trinity_Column_2006_conservation_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Holy_Trinity_Column_2006_conservation_3.jpg/500px-Holy_Trinity_Column_2006_conservation_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Revision and conservation of the Holy Trinity Column in Olomouc (Czech Republic) in 2006","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHoly_Trinity_Column_2006_conservation_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Clo%C3%AEtre_Saint-Trophime_Arles_Conservation.jpg/500px-Clo%C3%AEtre_Saint-Trophime_Arles_Conservation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Clo%C3%AEtre_Saint-Trophime_Arles_Conservation.jpg/1280px-Clo%C3%AEtre_Saint-Trophime_Arles_Conservation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Clo%C3%AEtre_Saint-Trophime_Arles_Conservation.jpg/500px-Clo%C3%AEtre_Saint-Trophime_Arles_Conservation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A temporary windowed partition along restoration work area in the cloister of the Church of St. Trophime, Arles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AClo%C3%AEtre_Saint-Trophime_Arles_Conservation.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Bixi_stele_%28wrapped%29%2C_Harvard_University%2C_Cambridge%2C_MA_-_IMG_4607.JPG/500px-Bixi_stele_%28wrapped%29%2C_Harvard_University%2C_Cambridge%2C_MA_-_IMG_4607.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Bixi_stele_%28wrapped%29%2C_Harvard_University%2C_Cambridge%2C_MA_-_IMG_4607.JPG/1280px-Bixi_stele_%28wrapped%29%2C_Harvard_University%2C_Cambridge%2C_MA_-_IMG_4607.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Bixi_stele_%28wrapped%29%2C_Harvard_University%2C_Cambridge%2C_MA_-_IMG_4607.JPG/500px-Bixi_stele_%28wrapped%29%2C_Harvard_University%2C_Cambridge%2C_MA_-_IMG_4607.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&